#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:27
#: f92eb4800eba48d4ba7164dab6a1b050
msgid "Powering the autopilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:29
#: ef114d55b224467e98c5293185b5906c
msgid ""
"The easiest way to power the APM2.x is using a :ref:`3DR Power Module "
"<common-3dr-power-module>` with a LiPo battery."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:32
#: 6790d07634a848eca2280e928256c1e8
msgid ""
"To wire a power module, connect the red-and-black two wire cable on the "
"power module to the PDB red and black two-wire. Connect the power module "
"to the APM PM port using a 6-position cable. Connect the PDB multi-wire "
"cable to APM Output Signal pins with the M1 wire connecting to the signal"
" pin labeled 1, M6 and signal pin 6, etc. See the above link for "
"additional detail."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:42
#: cdd4bc6f06b34be49bd78b6eb83e799e
msgid ""
"The Power Module will not power servos and other peripherals. For more "
"information/alternatives see :ref:`Powering the APM2 <common-powering-"
"the-apm2>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:46
#: dcf9c6506a164468ab2f75e4a9829752
msgid "Connect ESCs and motors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:48
#: 10f4fc3b30a64c4db2232656093e43a7
msgid ""
":ref:`Connecting the ESCs and Motors <connect-escs-and-motors>` explains "
"how to set up the connections, and the motor configuration setup for each"
" frame."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:52
#: 09a4115aa0e4485faf93c98a0525d5d1
msgid ""
"You will need to connect motor cables to electronic speed controller "
"(ESC) bullet connectors (each motor must connect to only one ESC)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/connecting-the-apm2.rst:58
#: ece4d1db37be4d9590278341f1315876
msgid ""
"Connect ESC Deans connectors to Power Distribution Board (PDB) Deans "
"connectors. Connect three-wire cables from the ESCs to the PDB signal "
"pins according to motor number (see link above to find the motor number "
"configuration for your frame). Connect the ESC for motor 1 to the PDB "
"pins marked M1, motor 6's ESC to the pins marked M6, etc."
msgstr ""

